{"reference":"Jeremiah 44","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":44,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Narrative","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 44 stands within the book’s account of Judah’s crisis under Babylonian domination: the destruction of Jerusalem, the events involving Gedaliah, and the flight to Egypt. This setting explains why the chapter addresses a remnant of Judah living in Egypt and recalls Jerusalem’s desolation as an already visible reality.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_044_ddc37c8d3f963058c8ffbab5"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}